---
name: Read HarfangLab events from the S3 export
description: |
  Watches the bucket of the HarfangLab S3 export for new objects, returns the
  OCSF events in them, and moves each object out of the watched prefix after
  reading it, so that a restart doesn't read it again.
---

// The S3 export writes a new gzip-compressed NDJSON object about every minute,
// named after its creation time in milliseconds, for example
// `harfanglab/1767225600000.json.gz`. The export also writes an empty
// `test-connection` object, which the glob skips.
//
// `from_s3` keeps no state across restarts and reads every matching object
// again on start. Moving read objects to `processed/` keeps them in the bucket
// as an archive while the watched prefix holds only new ones. This requires
// permission to write and delete objects in the bucket.
from_s3 "s3://example-bucket/harfanglab/*.json.gz",
  watch=1min,
  rename=(path => f"processed/{path}") {
  decompress_gzip
  read_ndjson
}
